# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS HERE
# ---------------------
# Two concrete problems existed before this file:
#
#   1. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` runs on `windows-latest` as part of the
#      `lint` job. With no normalisation in place, git hands the Windows runner
#      whatever the working tree happens to contain. The day someone commits
#      from Windows with CRLF checkouts enabled, every `.rs` file in the tree is
#      a formatting diff on that one leg only — a failure that reproduces for
#      nobody else and that `cargo fmt` cannot fix, because rustfmt does not
#      rewrite line endings of code it is not changing.
#
#   2. `cargo package` tars the working tree into the published `.crate`. The
#      contents of that archive must be byte-stable across machines, or the
#      same commit produces two different artefacts depending on who built it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text using its own heuristics; `eol=lf`
# then forces the LF form in the working tree for everything it classified as
# text. The result is identical bytes for every contributor on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Audio fixtures and other payloads that must never be touched.
#
# The decode corpus under `testdata/fixtures/` is generated by
# `scripts/make_fixtures.sh` and byte-compared against expectations, and the
# `fixtures` CI job fails if regeneration drifts. Without `binary`, git's
# newline heuristics could rewrite a CRLF byte pair inside a `.wav` header and
# silently change what the decoder sees.
*.wav binary
*.wv binary
*.opus binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.m4a binary
*.mp3 binary
*.aiff binary

# Opus conformance vectors (`crates/opus-decoder/tests/common.rs`). These are
# raw `opus_demo` framing and raw 16-bit PCM: a lone 0x0D is data, not a line
# ending, and the test vectors are pinned by checksum.
*.bit binary
*.dec binary

# Images (docs, HRTF plots, fixture screenshots).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# Archives that must round-trip byte-exact.
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary

# Manifests and sources, stated explicitly so a future `* text=auto` change
# cannot quietly relax them.
*.rs   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf diff=bash

# `Cargo.lock` is committed and is the reproducibility contract; make sure a
# merge never rewrites its line endings and turns the `supply-chain` job's
# `git diff --quiet -- Cargo.lock` gate into a false positive.
Cargo.lock text eol=lf

# `.gitattributes` and `.gitignore` themselves.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf